WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:09.071
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:15.460
Unit three: Family Relationships. Today you will talk about past family habits using used to.

4
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.401
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.739
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:24.422
Guardian.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:28.287
Guardian means a person who legally looks after a child.

8
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:30.372
My aunt is my guardian.

9
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:33.752
Your turn. Say: Guardian.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.636
Guardian.

11
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.268
Discipline.

12
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:43.247
Discipline means training people to follow rules.

13
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.453
My father's discipline taught me good habits.

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.691
Your turn. Say: Discipline.

15
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:53.407
Discipline.

16
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:54.977
Supportive.

17
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:58.575
Supportive means helpful and encouraging.

18
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:01.044
My parents are always supportive.

19
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.163
Your turn. Say: Supportive.

20
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.036
Supportive.

21
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:09.680
Argument.

22
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:13.948
Argument means an angry talk between people who disagree.

23
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.573
We had an argument about the TV.

24
00:01:17.183 --> 00:01:19.522
Your turn. Say: Argument.

25
00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:23.217
Argument.

26
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.019
Compromise.

27
00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:29.154
Compromise means an agreement where each side gives a little.

28
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.249
We made a compromise: one hour each.

29
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.827
Your turn. Say: Compromise.

30
00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:39.877
Compromise.

31
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:41.676
Respect.

32
00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:45.623
Respect means thinking that someone is important and good.

33
00:01:46.217 --> 00:01:48.448
We show respect to our grandparents.

34
00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.027
Your turn. Say: Respect.

35
00:01:54.867 --> 00:01:55.891
Respect.

36
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:57.883
Understanding.

37
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:01.579
Understanding means knowing how someone feels.

38
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:04.334
My mother shows great understanding.

39
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.776
Your turn. Say: Understanding.

40
00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:11.832
Understanding.

41
00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:13.770
Sacrifice.

42
00:02:14.783 --> 00:02:17.955
Sacrifice means giving up something for someone else.

43
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.258
My parents made a sacrifice for my education.

44
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:24.351
Your turn. Say: Sacrifice.

45
00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.549
Sacrifice.

46
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:30.180
Tradition.

47
00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:34.274
Tradition means a custom passed down over many years.

48
00:02:34.883 --> 00:02:37.417
Visiting the pagoda is a family tradition.

49
00:02:38.017 --> 00:02:40.286
Your turn. Say: Tradition.

50
00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.065
Tradition.

51
00:02:44.817 --> 00:02:45.620
Bond.

52
00:02:46.617 --> 00:02:49.406
Bond means a strong feeling that connects people.

53
00:02:50.017 --> 00:02:52.202
I have a close bond with my grandfather.

54
00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:55.527
Your turn. Say: Bond.

55
00:02:58.367 --> 00:02:59.019
Bond.

56
00:02:59.783 --> 00:03:00.982
Quality time.

57
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:05.573
Quality time means time spent giving full attention to someone.

58
00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:08.868
We spend quality time together on Sundays.

59
00:03:09.483 --> 00:03:11.962
Your turn. Say: Quality time.

60
00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.173
Quality time.

61
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:18.104
Reconcile.

62
00:03:19.117 --> 00:03:22.602
Reconcile means to become friends again after a disagreement.

63
00:03:23.217 --> 00:03:25.367
After the argument, we reconciled.

64
00:03:25.983 --> 00:03:28.740
Your turn. Say: Reconcile.

65
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.857
Reconcile.

66
00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:37.735
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:38.583 --> 00:03:41.674
Visal, how does your family solve disagreements?

68
00:03:42.783 --> 00:03:44.945
We talk and try to make a compromise.

69
00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.713
Was it always like that?

70
00:03:48.817 --> 00:03:52.630
No. My brother and I used to argue a lot.

71
00:03:53.717 --> 00:03:54.753
What changed?

72
00:03:55.850 --> 00:04:02.067
My grandmother taught us respect. Now we reconcile quickly and spend more quality time together.

73
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.805
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:08.660
Grammar focus: used to for past habits.

75
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.170
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.372
We used to argue a lot.

77
00:04:13.283 --> 00:04:15.585
I used to live with my grandparents.

78
00:04:16.483 --> 00:04:18.669
Did you use to fight with your sister?

79
00:04:19.633 --> 00:04:24.968
Use 'used to' for past habits that are not true now. In questions and negatives, write 'use to'.

80
00:04:25.717 --> 00:04:29.089
Be careful! Don't say: We use to argue a lot.

81
00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:33.091
Say: We used to argue a lot.

82
00:04:33.391 --> 00:04:35.936
In positive sentences, write 'used to'.

83
00:04:36.733 --> 00:04:39.339
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.796
Learning to Compromise.

85
00:04:42.096 --> 00:04:45.524
My guardian shows discipline, but also great understanding.

86
00:04:46.533 --> 00:04:50.100
My sister and I used to have an argument almost every day.

87
00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.679
Now, after an argument, we always try to compromise and reconcile.

88
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:58.700
We respect the sacrifices our family makes for us.

89
00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:04.314
Every Sunday, we spend quality time together. It is our tradition.

90
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:09.367
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:10.217 --> 00:05:12.379
We blank argue a lot, but now we don't.

92
00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:16.216
A, used to. B, use. C, using to.

93
00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.592
The answer is A: used to.

94
00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.760
An agreement where each side gives a little is a blank.

95
00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:30.154
A, compromise. B, sacrifice. C, guardian.

96
00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.839
The answer is A: compromise.

97
00:05:36.983 --> 00:05:39.958
To become friends again after a disagreement is to blank.

98
00:05:40.258 --> 00:05:43.807
A, reconcile. B, respect. C, argue.

99
00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.401
The answer is A: reconcile.

100
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.740
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:57.326
How does your family resolve disagreements?

102
00:06:06.117 --> 00:06:07.512
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:07.812 --> 00:06:15.771
We sit down and talk calmly. We used to shout, but now we listen to each other and find a compromise.

104
00:06:16.071 --> 00:06:17.861
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:23.504
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and used to for past habits.

106
00:06:23.804 --> 00:06:28.523
Today's value is understanding. Listen first, and try to see how others feel.

107
00:06:28.823 --> 00:06:31.452
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

108
00:06:31.752 --> 00:06:34.683
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

